You don't have to lift
the seats in and out.

137
00:07:48,567 --> 00:07:51,100
它们能直接折进地板里，
然后你只要这么……
They just fold in the floor
and then you just sort of...

138
00:07:51,733 --> 00:07:53,600
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

139
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:56,867
提起来就行了。
往上提啊，你个蠢货！
You just lift it out.
You lift it out, you fool!

140
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:59,033
-（座椅咔嗒声）
-哈蒙德：得，卡死了。
-(SEAT RATTLES)
-HAMMOND: Yeah, that's truck.

141
00:07:59,067 --> 00:08:00,533
克拉克森：
现场有谁开赛飞利吗？
CLARKSON:
Has anybody got a Zafira?

142
00:08:00,567 --> 00:08:02,100
台下女观众：你得先把
后排座椅往前推。
WOMAN IN AUDIENCE: You move
the back seats forward.

143
00:08:02,133 --> 00:08:03,900
-两人异口同声：啥？
-女观众：先把
后排座椅往前推。
-BOTH: What?
-WOMAN: You move
the back seats forward.

144
00:08:03,933 --> 00:08:05,367
两人：我们早就知道了！
BOTH: We knew that!

145
00:08:05,467 --> 00:08:07,367
把后排座椅往前推。
Move the back seats forward.

146
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:09,467
（大笑）
(LAUGHING)

147
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:12,033
-可是……
-克拉克森：拉手在哪儿？
-But...
-CLARKSON: Where's the lever?

148
00:08:12,067 --> 00:08:13,467
哈蒙德：（砸座椅声）
砸它可不管用。
HAMMOND: (THUMPING)
That doesn't help.

149
00:08:13,467 --> 00:08:15,100
克拉克森：不好意思，
拉手到底在哪儿？
CLARKSON: Excuse me,
where's the lever?

150
00:08:15,133 --> 00:08:16,800
-台下女观众：
座椅后面！
-哈蒙德：是那个吗？
-WOMAN IN AUDIENCE:
Behind the seat!
-HAMMOND: That one?

151
00:08:16,833 --> 00:08:18,667
对，我们早就知道了。
Yeah, we knew that.

152
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:21,967
我们节目救动力漂移可是一绝，
但搞不定这玩意儿。
We're really good on this show
at controlling power slides,
but not this.

153
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:24,267
然后再把这些座椅
提起来。
And then you can just
lift these seats.

154
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:25,967
（哈蒙德狂笑）
(HAMMOND GUFFAWS)

155
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:29,700
太完蛋了！
太丢人了！
This is bad!
This is embarrassing!

156
00:08:29,733 --> 00:08:35,000
你一手拎着购物袋，
一手拿着儿童安全座椅……大力出奇迹……
暴力永远是解决问题的唯一真理。
You've got a shopping bag,
child seat, Brute force...
That's always the answer.

157
00:08:35,033 --> 00:08:36,833
（笑声与掌声）
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

158
00:08:36,867 --> 00:08:39,033
我好像把它给掰断了！
I might have broken that!

159
00:08:40,133 --> 00:08:42,500
等等。不好意思，你刚说
你有一辆赛飞利？
Hang on. Sorry, you said,
you've got a Zafira?

160
00:08:42,533 --> 00:08:44,100
（听不清）
(INDISTINCT)

161
00:08:44,133 --> 00:08:46,967
你能过来帮个忙吗？
我好像把它给掰坏了。
Could you just come
and give us a hand?
I've broken it.

162
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:50,567
不不不，是这儿，你看。
No, no, no. It's this. Look.

163
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,233
女士：没错，你确实把它弄坏了。
WOMAN: Yeah, you have
broken that.

164
00:08:52,267 --> 00:08:53,633
（观众笑声）
((AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

165
00:08:54,767 --> 00:08:56,000
那个本来应该卡在下面的。
That should lock under there.

166
00:08:56,033 --> 00:08:57,733
你在沃克斯豪尔4S店上过班吗？
Have you worked
in a Vauxhall dealership?

167
00:08:57,767 --> 00:08:59,733
-女士：搞定！
-多谢！
-WOMAN: There you go!
-Thank you!

168
00:08:59,767 --> 00:09:01,467
（欢呼声与掌声）
(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

169
00:09:01,467 --> 00:09:05,000
这可真……呃，
太丢人了。（笑）
That's, um,
quite embarrassing. (LAUGHS)

170
00:09:05,967 --> 00:09:08,333
哈蒙德：伙计，我觉得自己像个傻子。（笑）
HAMMOND: I feel
a bit silly, mate. (LAUGHING)

171
00:09:08,367 --> 00:09:10,300
克拉克森：
是啊。我这就来……
CLARKSON:
Yeah. I'm going to just...

172
00:09:10,333 --> 00:09:13,133
啊，这就对了！
行了，没错。
Ah, there you go!
That's it, yeah.

173
00:09:14,567 --> 00:09:15,733
立起来了。
That's up.

174
00:09:15,767 --> 00:09:17,800
问题是，
一旦你弄好了这个，
The thing is,
once you've done that,

175
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:20,100
你看，你还得钻到里面去。
look, you've got
to get in there.

176
00:09:20,133 --> 00:09:21,800
这简直是……
连我都钻不进去！
Which is...
Even I couldn't get in there!

177
00:09:21,833 --> 00:09:23,500
-根本不可能，而且后备厢太小了。
-根本就没有后备厢好吗。
-Impossible and the boot's
far too small.
-There isn't any boot.

178
00:09:23,533 --> 00:09:26,133
但换成福特，
就完全没这些破毛病了。
But you don't get
any of those problems
with the Ford.

179
00:09:26,167 --> 00:09:27,733
因为这台我已经试过了。
'Cause I have had a go
with this one.

180
00:09:27,767 --> 00:09:29,567
差不多的设计，但好用得多。
Similar system, but better.

181
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:33,600
打开后备厢，
只要把坐垫拎起来，
一、二……
Open the boot,
you just lift the seat squabs,
one, two...

182
00:09:33,633 --> 00:09:39,700
像这样，靠背拉起，
往下放，瞧好了……
七个座，齐活了。
Like that, up with the back,
down, and there you go...
Seven seats, all in place.

183
00:09:39,733 --> 00:09:41,533
而且……更绝的是，你看。
And...and what's more, look.

184
00:09:41,567 --> 00:09:45,500
手里提着一大堆沉东西回来，
只要拉一下拉杆，座椅往前滑，
Come back with your
heavy shopping, just one lever
slides that forwards

185
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:46,933
你就能坐进去了。
and then you can get in.

186
00:09:46,967 --> 00:09:48,500
不仅如此，
你还有一个正经的后备厢空间。
Not only that,
you've got a proper
boot space.

187
00:09:48,533 --> 00:09:49,667
其实是有两个。
Actually, you've got two.

188
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:51,467
底下有一块暗格，
还有后备厢本身。
There's a bit under there
and the actual boot.

189
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:54,633
你甚至能把Top Gear……
说真的，我去抱她过来。
来啦，谢啦。
You could get Top Gear...
In fact, I'll get her.
Here she is, thank you.

190
00:09:54,667 --> 00:09:55,933
过来，Top Gear狗！
Come on, Top Gear Dog!

191
00:09:55,967 --> 00:09:57,267
克拉克森：Top Gear狗
要塞进后备厢？
CLARKSON: Top Gear Dog
going in the boot?

192
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:59,100
她不想去后面，来嘛……
She won't go in the back,
come on...

193
00:09:59,133 --> 00:10:00,367
克拉克森：
Top Gear狗总算派上用场了！
CLARKSON:
Top Gear Dog has a use!

194
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:02,200
看吧，她在里面待得多舒坦。
There, see she can go in there
quite happily.

195
00:10:02,233 --> 00:10:05,000
本节目拍摄过程中没有犬只受到伤害。
No dogs were harmed in
the making of this programme.

196
00:10:05,033 --> 00:10:06,933
-把头抬起来，把头抬起来。好啦！
-好啦！
-Put you head up.
Put you head up. There!
-There!

197
00:10:06,967 --> 00:10:08,433
（笑声与掌声）
(LAUGHTER AND APPLAUSE)

198
00:10:08,467 --> 00:10:10,833
-克拉克森：太省事了。
-哈蒙德：你看，管用吧。
-CLARKSON: It's easy.
-HAMMOND: You see, it works.

199
00:10:10,867 --> 00:10:12,767
在赛飞利上你可办不到这个。
And you can't do that
in the Zafira.

200
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:16,200
我必须得说，
这车真特么是辆好车。
I have to say, this is
one hell of a good car.

201
00:10:16,233 --> 00:10:17,900
没错。
我们得出结论了。
Oh, yeah.
We've got a conclusion.

202
00:10:17,933 --> 00:10:20,133
基本上，福特是最实用的，
这点我们已经证明了。
Basically, the Ford is
the most practical,
we've shown that.

203
00:10:20,167 --> 00:10:22,133
它在赛道上不是最快的，
但放到现实生活中，
It's not the fastest
around the track,
but in the real world,

204
00:10:22,167 --> 00:10:24,133
它开起来最过瘾，
长得也最帅，
it's the best one to drive,
it's the best-looking,

205
00:10:24,167 --> 00:10:26,300
而且你要是买乞丐版，
它还是最便宜的。
and if you get the basic one,
it's the cheapest.

206
00:10:26,333 --> 00:10:28,867
所以，结论就是这样。
那现在，来看新闻。
So, there we are.
So, now, let's do the news.

207
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:33,967
好，先来一条好消息——
MG（名爵）复活了……
算是吧。
Yes and we begin with
good news, which is that
MG is back... Sort of.

208
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,800
实际情况是这样的，
What's actually happened is

209
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:38,633
买下MG罗孚品牌商标权的
那家中国公司，
that the Chinese company
that has bought the rights
to the MG Rover name

210
00:10:38,667 --> 00:10:41,367
宣布要重新开启长桥工厂，
has said that it will reopen
the Longbridge factory,

211
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:44,667
而且明年就要
重新投产MG TF。
and that next year, it will
start making the MG TF again.

212
00:10:44,700 --> 00:10:48,133
等等，先打住。
他们难道不是打算先在中国造好，
Well, hold on a minute.
Aren't they going to
make it in China,

213
00:10:48,167 --> 00:10:50,100
再拆成零件运到这边，
then take it to pieces,
then ship it over here,

214
00:10:50,133 --> 00:10:52,833
然后在伯明翰拼装起来，
好吹嘘这是英国造的？
and then assemble it
in Birmingham,
so they can say it's British?

215
00:10:52,867 --> 00:10:55,167
-他们打的不就是这算盘吗？
-没错，按我们的理解确实是这样。
-Isn't that the idea?
-Yes, that's as we
understand it.

216
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:58,933
但你想想看，
中国人声称他们打算
But if you think about this,
the Chinese, they say
they're going to be investing

217
00:10:58,967 --> 00:11:01,467
-给长桥工厂投资一千万英镑，对吧？
-克拉克森：对。
-£10 million in Longbridge,
yeah?
-CLARKSON: Yeah.

218
00:11:01,467 --> 00:11:05,233
这钱确实不少……
要是拿去买糖吃的话。
Well, that's a lot of money...
If you're going to
spend it on sweets.

219
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:07,167
但我特意做过一点调查。
But I've done some
research on this.

220
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:13,500
说真的，奔驰光是搞研发，
每天就得烧掉一千万英镑。
Seriously. Mercedes spent
£10 million on research alone
every single day.

221
00:11:13,533 --> 00:11:15,000
所以那一千万能顶什么用？
So where's that
going to go?

222
00:11:15,033 --> 00:11:17,067
而且人家奔驰最后造出来的车你还想买。
And they end up with cars
that you might want to buy.

223
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:19,467
我认识的人里，找不出任何一个会琢磨：
I can't think of anyone I've
ever met who thinks,

224
00:11:19,467 --> 00:11:21,200
“对啊，我的人生就圆满了，
"Yes, my life
would be complete

225
00:11:21,233 --> 00:11:25,633
“只要能买到一辆在中国造的
11年老款跑车，
"if I could buy an 11-year-old
sports car that's made
in China

226
00:11:25,667 --> 00:11:28,833
“再由伯明翰的一帮糙汉
拿钉子胡乱拼凑起来。”
"and then nailed together by
a bunch of blokes
in Birmingham."

227
00:11:28,867 --> 00:11:32,133
你忽略了一点，
那就是全世界人民
The thing that
you are forgetting is
the great affection

228
00:11:32,167 --> 00:11:37,333
对传统英伦跑车
怀有的那种深厚情怀。
that is felt all over
the world for the traditional
British sports car.

229
00:11:37,367 --> 00:11:39,467
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGH)

230
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:44,133
嘿，我这周也有关于我自己的
重磅汽车新闻。
Hey, I've got big
motoring news
this week of my own.

231
00:11:44,167 --> 00:11:46,000
买了辆新家用车，激动坏了。
Bought a new family car.
Very excited.

232
00:11:46,033 --> 00:11:48,633
我买了辆二手的路虎卫士，
就是大号厢式旅行版那种。
I bought a second-hand
Land Rover Defender.
Big station wagon thing.

233
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:52,000
还是个特别版，亮黄色的，
现在早就不产了。
It's a special edition.
It's bright yellow.
They don't make it any more.

234
00:11:52,033 --> 00:11:56,033
而且正因为停产了，
他们随车还送了一罐黄油漆，
And because they don't make it
any more they gave us a pot of
yellow paint to go with it,

235
00:11:56,067 --> 00:11:57,567
用来补补划痕——这可是新车啊！
to touch out any scratches
new car!

236
00:11:57,600 --> 00:12:00,567
提车第一天，全家蜂拥而上，
直接扎了进去……全家都上了车。
First day in it, family piled
in. Dove right...family in.

237
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:01,900
开着新车去开启全新冒险。
A new adventure in a new car.

238
00:12:01,933 --> 00:12:03,700
刚开出两英里，
Two miles down the road,

239
00:12:03,733 --> 00:12:06,167
“走，开着咱的新车去加油站，
完成第一次加油！”
"Let's go for our first
fill-up in a petrol station
in our new car."

240
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:11,100
正要左转，我转头一瞧，
只见我老婆手里正端着那罐油漆，
Went to turn left. I looked
across and saw my wife
holding the pot of paint,

241
00:12:11,133 --> 00:12:14,033
肯定是因为天太热，
里面憋足了气还是怎么着
that must have pressurised
in the heat or something

242
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:17,733
结果除了她那双眼睛，
浑身上下全黄了。
because everything apart
from her eyes,
everything was yellow.

243
00:12:17,767 --> 00:12:22,767
地毯、车顶棚，
全都在往下滴……
挡风玻璃也是一片蜡黄。
The carpet, the ceiling,
all dripping off...
The windscreen all yellow.

244
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:26,800
看着就跟青春期少年的梳妆镜似的，
简直彻底毁了！
It looked like
a teenager's mirror.
It was just ruined!

245
00:12:26,833 --> 00:12:28,300
就在那儿滴答、滴答地淌……
It was just drip, drip...

246
00:12:28,333 --> 00:12:30,867
这周我开着我的福特GT，
搞了次家庭出游。
I had a family outing
this week in my Ford GT.

247
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:33,533
带我儿子去了格洛斯特郡的
费尔福德航展。
Took my son to
the Fairford Airshow,
Gloucestershire.

248
00:12:33,567 --> 00:12:34,667
然后呢？
And?

249
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,567
车现在还扔在那儿呢。
It's still there.

250
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,567
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

251
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:42,600
限转器自作主张，
死活不肯让发动机转速
超过600转，
Rev Limiter decided that it
didn't want to let the engine
to rev beyond 600 rpm,

252
00:12:42,633 --> 00:12:43,767
这转速可不算高。
which isn't much.

253
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,767
压根就不够让车
往前挪半步的。
Not enough
to actually make progress.

254
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:49,200
噢，对了，最近这几周
陆陆续续冒出了几款新车。
Oh, now, there are some
new cars that have been
coming out in recent weeks.

255
00:12:49,233 --> 00:12:52,333
有这款全新本田思域Type R，
那边有张照片。
There's this new
Honda Civic Type R,
got a photograph there.

256
00:12:52,367 --> 00:12:55,700
你瞧这模样，就知道
这车开起来肯定棒极了。
If you look at that, you know
that's going to be
a great car to drive.

257
00:12:55,733 --> 00:12:57,633
光看长相心里就有数了，对吧。
You just know
by looking at it, okay.

258
00:12:57,667 --> 00:12:59,100
还有新款路虎神行者。
There's a new
Land Rover Freelander.

259
00:12:59,133 --> 00:13:02,500
同样，瞅它一眼，
你就知道这车绝对靠谱。
Again, look at that,
you know it's all
gonna be fine.

260
00:13:02,533 --> 00:13:04,833
还有克莱斯勒新车，
叫Sebring。
New Chrysler.
It's called the Sebring.

261
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,967
你瞅它一眼就知道，
这货绝对是坨工业垃圾！
You look at that and you know
it'll be rubbish!

262
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:08,467
哈蒙德：（笑）
绝对是，可不是嘛！
HAMMOND: (LAUGHING)
It will be, won't it?

263
00:13:08,467 --> 00:13:11,100
你就知道他们心虚得不行……
我翻了翻产品资料。
You know they're in trouble...
I was reading the details.

264
00:13:11,133 --> 00:13:13,233
他们就给这车
寄来了一页纸的介绍。
They sent us
a one-page thing on that car.

265
00:13:13,267 --> 00:13:16,267
整整一页纸，要罗列完
这辆车所有的“亮点”！
One page to get all the things
about that car!

266
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:18,067
看到半当中，
他们居然在吹嘘
Halfway down,
they're talking about

267
00:13:18,100 --> 00:13:20,467
开车的时候杯架
