at a certain speed.

392
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:21,733
车内某个角落肯定配有按钮，
让你能手动强制干预。
They've all got a button
somewhere inside,
so you can over-ride it.

393
00:21:21,767 --> 00:21:24,967
好嘛，你想升的时候再升起来。
但这台车偏不。
Okay, so, you can put it up
when you want it.
This doesn't.

394
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:28,533
那尾翼时速一到80英里就升起来，
不管你乐不乐意。
That spoiler comes up at 80,
whether you like it or not.

395
00:21:28,567 --> 00:21:32,000
简直就跟在车屁股上升了面旗子、
上面写着“老子超速了”没两样。
So, it might as well hoist
a flag on the back that says,
"I'm speeding."

396
00:21:32,033 --> 00:21:33,733
克拉克森：一点没错。
CLARKSON: Exactly.

397
00:21:33,767 --> 00:21:37,500
现在，我们得看看这玩意儿
绕我们赛道一圈到底能跑多快了。
And now we've got to find out
how fast this goes
round our track.

398
00:21:37,533 --> 00:21:41,633
这当然就意味着，
得把它交给我们圈养的赛车手了。
That, of course,
means handing it over to
our tame racing driver.

399
00:21:41,667 --> 00:21:47,500
有人说，在酷热难耐的大热天里，
他会像蛇一样蜕皮；
Some say that on
really warm days, he sheds
his skin, like a snake,

400
00:21:47,533 --> 00:21:50,767
还有人说，不知出于什么原因，
他对荷兰人过敏。
and that, for some reason,
he's allergic to the Dutch.

401
00:21:50,800 --> 00:21:52,467
（众人大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

402
00:21:52,467 --> 00:21:55,633
我们只知道，
他叫斯提格。
All we know is,
he's called the Stig.

403
00:21:55,667 --> 00:21:57,167
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINE REVVING)

404
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:59,467
克拉克森：发车了！
CLARKSON: And he's off.

405
00:21:59,467 --> 00:22:01,867
起步冒出了一小缕胎烟，
但四驱系统很快就把它
收拾得服服帖帖。
Little plumes of tyre
smoke there but the four wheel
drive soon got that reined in.

406
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:03,467
来到第一个弯道……
Here's the first corner...

407
00:22:03,467 --> 00:22:06,133
看这入弯多干脆利落！
Look how keenly it turns in.

408
00:22:06,167 --> 00:22:07,733
现在他又一脚油门踩下去！
And now he's back
on the power.

409
00:22:07,767 --> 00:22:09,567
听听这声浪！
Listen to that!

410
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:12,333
-（磁带女声讲希腊语）
-男声：（翻译）
“有危险吗？”
-(WOMAN ON TAPE SPEAKS GREEK)
-MAN: (TRANSLATES)
"Is it dangerous?"

411
00:22:12,367 --> 00:22:15,167
克拉克森：
看来斯提格还在学希腊语呢！
CLARKSON:
Stig's still learning Greek,
it seems!

412
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:17,467
穿过芝加哥弯，他又冲过来了。
And meeting us again
through Chicago.

413
00:22:17,467 --> 00:22:20,000
甩起车尾，为杀进锤头弯
找好了绝佳走线。
Kicking the back out to give
him the perfect line down
to Hammerhead.

414
00:22:20,033 --> 00:22:21,633
他现在进弯了，
会推头吗？
That's where he is now.
at understeer?

415
00:22:21,667 --> 00:22:26,467
一点都没有！抓地力十足，
伴随着V10引擎的雷霆咆哮！
Not a bit of it! Loads of grip
and that V10 thunder.

416
00:22:26,467 --> 00:22:28,800
出弯这一下漂移太销魂了！
What a lovely drift
on the way out!

417
00:22:28,833 --> 00:22:31,233
（磁带女声讲希腊语）
(WOMAN ON TAPE SPEAKS GREEK)

418
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:34,033
男声：（翻译）
“我的钱包丢了。”
MAN: (TRANSLATES)
"I've lost my purse."

419
00:22:34,067 --> 00:22:35,700
克拉克森：
进入全速弯……
CLARKSON:
Follow through now...

420
00:22:35,733 --> 00:22:38,467
噢，他不得不迅速反打一把方向！
Oh, he's having to give it
a flick of opposite lock now!

421
00:22:38,467 --> 00:22:40,133
油门狠狠踩到底！
Hammer down hard.

422
00:22:40,167 --> 00:22:42,167
非常快！掠过轮胎墙。
还剩最后两个弯。
That's very quick.
Through the tyres.
Two corners left.

423
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:45,000
噢，切进那个弯了，
过弯动作极其凶狠决绝！
Oh, he goes into that one.
He's very committed
through there.

424
00:22:45,033 --> 00:22:47,933
重踩刹车，硬生生砸进甘榜弯！
Hard on the brakes.
Shoving it into Gambon.

425
00:22:47,967 --> 00:22:50,200
冲线！
And across the line!

426
00:22:50,233 --> 00:22:51,467
漂亮！
Yes!

427
00:22:53,767 --> 00:22:55,033
那么……
Now...

428
00:22:58,333 --> 00:23:03,067
成绩出炉：
1分25秒7……
It did it
in 1 minute 25.7 seconds...

429
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:07,100
虽然它算不上所谓的
世上最快的超跑，
So it's not what you'd call
the fastest super car
in the world,

430
00:23:07,133 --> 00:23:10,600
但我不得不承认，
它成了我的新欢。
but I have to say it is
my new favourite.

431
00:23:10,633 --> 00:23:13,933
接下来，又到了明星开廉价车环节！
And now it's time to put
a star in our reasonably
priced car.

432
00:23:13,967 --> 00:23:17,933
今晚的这位嘉宾，
曾经在80天内环游过地球。
Now, my guest tonight
once went round the world
in 80 days.

433
00:23:17,967 --> 00:23:20,600
我希望他在我们赛道上
能比那次快点！
I hope he's faster than that
on our track!

434
00:23:20,633 --> 00:23:23,533
女士们先生们，
掌声欢迎史蒂夫·库根！
Ladies and gentlemen,
please welcome Steve Coogan!

435
00:23:39,533 --> 00:23:42,900
啊，自打你上次来过之后，
如今可成了好莱坞大腕了啊。
Ah, now, since you were
last here, you've become
the big Hollywood star.

436
00:23:42,933 --> 00:23:44,467
算不上，真没有。
Not really, no.

437
00:23:44,500 --> 00:23:45,700
克拉克森：得了吧，怎么不是！
CLARKSON: Well, yes!

438
00:23:45,733 --> 00:23:47,200
我努力过啦。
I've tried.

439
00:23:47,233 --> 00:23:48,533
你确实拍过好几部
好莱坞大片呢。
You have appeared
in a number of
Hollywood films.

440
00:23:48,567 --> 00:23:49,667
那倒是。
Yeah.

441
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:51,000
克里斯早就料到会这样了，
对吧？
Cleese knew this'd happen.
Didn't he?

442
00:23:51,033 --> 00:23:52,933
约翰·克里斯当年
到底跟你说了什么？
What did John Cleese
once say to you?

443
00:23:52,967 --> 00:23:59,233
噢，对。我以前和……额，
约翰·克里斯还有特里·琼斯
拍过一部电影……
Oh, yeah. I did a film with,
um, John Cleese
and Terry Jones...

444
00:23:59,267 --> 00:24:00,900
片名叫
《柳林风声》。
It was called
Wind In The Willows.

445
00:24:00,933 --> 00:24:03,667
当时呢，
我有一辆红色法拉利。
At the time,
I had a red Ferrari.

446
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:05,633
就是《夏威夷神探》同款的那种风格。
The Magnum, P.I. style.

447
00:24:05,667 --> 00:24:07,367
额……所以才穿了这件花衬衫！
Um...hence the shirt!

448
00:24:07,467 --> 00:24:08,900
（笑声）
(LAUGHING)

449
00:24:08,933 --> 00:24:11,967
约翰·克里斯看见我开着它走，
And John Cleese saw me
driving off in it,

450
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:17,067
他就问制片人，
他说：“开那辆法拉利的
是谁啊？”
and he said to the producer,
he went, "Who was
driving that Ferrari?"

451
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:19,000
制片人说：
“那是史蒂夫·库根。”
He went,
"That's Steve Coogan."

452
00:24:19,033 --> 00:24:23,200
“他可是个非常有才华的
年轻小伙，对吧？”
"He's a very, very talented
young man, isn't he?"

453
00:24:23,233 --> 00:24:24,700
制片人说：“没错，确实是。”
And he went, "Yeah, he is."

454
00:24:24,733 --> 00:24:26,467
“我真希望他早点得癌症。”
"I do hope he gets cancer."

455
00:24:26,500 --> 00:24:28,100
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

456
00:24:29,567 --> 00:24:33,267
说句掏心窝子的大实话，
我可太眼红你的人生了。
I'm quite envious
of how your life's turned out,
to be brutally honest.

457
00:24:33,300 --> 00:24:35,467
因为你不管搞什么，
好像都能顺风顺水赚大钱。
'Cause everything you ever do
seems to turn to gold.

458
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:38,500
额，其实我也翻车过几次……
不过嘛，嗯……
Um, I've had a few misses...
But, um, yeah...

459
00:24:38,533 --> 00:24:41,033
-但你翻车的时候往往也挺爽的。
-噢，那倒是，那倒是。
-You always have a nice time
while having the misses.
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

460
00:24:41,067 --> 00:24:43,233
就比如我拍《环游地球八十天》那会儿，
I mean, when I did
Around The World In 80 Days,

461
00:24:43,267 --> 00:24:44,700
戏里有一幕是我在泡按摩浴缸。
there was a scene in the film
where I was in a Jacuzzi.

462
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:47,133
当时我坐在成龙和阿诺德·施瓦辛格中间，
And I sat between Jackie Chan
and Arnold Schwarzenegger,

463
00:24:47,167 --> 00:24:49,567
夹成了一个“成龙-施瓦辛格”
三明治。
in a Chan-Schwarzenegger
sandwich.

464
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:51,033
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

465
00:24:51,067 --> 00:24:53,533
我当时都不知道该……
额，反正就是没话找话。
And I didn't know what to...
Uh, it was my small talk.

466
00:24:53,567 --> 00:24:57,467
我问他：“阿诺德，
你平时还开你那辆悍马吗？”
I said, "Are you still driving
your Hummer, Arnold?"

467
00:24:57,467 --> 00:24:59,300
（模仿施瓦辛格）
“开啊，我有五辆呢！”
(IMITATING SCHWARZENEGGER)
"Yes, I have five!"

468
00:24:59,333 --> 00:25:01,500
（大笑）
(LAUGHING)

469
00:25:01,533 --> 00:25:04,467
他说：
“对，其中一辆是军用款，
退役军车，内饰全拆空了。
He said,
"Yes, one is military,
ex-military, stripped out.

470
00:25:04,467 --> 00:25:08,467
“我就喜欢叼着雪茄，
开着它在洛杉矶到处晃。”
"I like to drive it round LA,
with my cigar."

471
00:25:08,467 --> 00:25:12,467
到底是怎么聊的，
才会沦落到
跟你共泡一个热水浴缸啊？
How does the conversation go,
to end up
in a hot tub with you?

472
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:14,633
“快到浴缸里来
跟我一起泡，史蒂夫。”
"Get in the hot tub
with me, Steve."

473
00:25:14,667 --> 00:25:16,533
-（大笑）
-克拉克森：还真像。
-(LAUGHING)
-CLARKSON: Yes.

474
00:25:16,567 --> 00:25:17,833
差不多就是这套路。
It was something like that.

475
00:25:17,867 --> 00:25:19,900
-克拉克森：
差不多是这套路？
-对。
-CLARKSON:
Something like that?
-Yeah.

476
00:25:19,933 --> 00:25:22,767
（观众鼓掌）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

477
00:25:23,767 --> 00:25:27,233
呵，你们这帮人还真容易满足，
不是吗？
Huh, you're easily pleased,
aren't you?

478
00:25:27,267 --> 00:25:29,633
言归正传，《萨克森戴尔》是你的
新剧。
Anyway, Saxondale's your
new series.

479
00:25:29,667 --> 00:25:31,167
这个角色是……
This is a character who is...

480
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:35,833
他是个五十岁的
前摇滚巡演后勤，
后来转行当了灭虫员。
He's a 50-year-old
ex-roadie
turned-pest-controller.

481
00:25:36,733 --> 00:25:38,167
到处都是这种人。
There's a lot of them around.

482
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:41,033
重点是，我看第二集的时候，
The thing is, I was watching
the second episode,

483
00:25:41,067 --> 00:25:45,733
你演的那个萨克森代尔去找一个汽车记者……
when your man Saxondale
goes to see
a motoring journalist...

484
00:25:45,767 --> 00:25:48,267
（笑声）
(LAUGHING)

485
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:50,600
……那家伙也主持着一档汽车电视节目。
...who's got this
TV show about cars.

486
00:25:50,633 --> 00:25:51,967
嗯。
Hmm.

487
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:54,700
我们要不要看一小段那个片段？
Shall we have a look
at a little clip of that?

488
00:25:54,733 --> 00:25:57,467
一起来看下这段，请看。
Let's have a look
at this, okay.

489
00:25:57,467 --> 00:25:59,467
（门铃响）
(DOORBELL RINGS)

490
00:26:00,467 --> 00:26:02,267
嗨，来抓老鼠的消杀人员？
Hi. Pest control for the mice?

491
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:03,567
正是我们。
The very same.

492
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:05,533
太棒了。二位快请进吧，绅士们。
Eccellente. Shimmy on in,
then, gents.

493
00:26:05,567 --> 00:26:10,200
我能先耽搁一下，向房主脱帽致个敬吗，
Can I just halt proceedings
to doff the proverbial
to the guv'nor,

494
00:26:10,233 --> 00:26:11,467
就冲院里那台座驾？
re. the wheels?

495
00:26:12,300 --> 00:26:14,033
R-E-S-P-E-C-T，大写的敬佩。
R, E, S, P, E, C, T.

496
00:26:14,067 --> 00:26:15,633
~没错，佩服。
~好说，承让。
-Yeah, respect.
-Right. Yeah.

497
00:26:15,667 --> 00:26:17,167
你也是懂车的行家？
Are you an aficionado?

498
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,567
车道上停了辆野马。
Got a Mustang in the drive.

499
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:19,667
噢，谢尔比？
Oh, Shelby?

500
00:26:19,700 --> 00:26:22,133
想得美！不是，是Boss 351。
I wish! No, Boss 351.

501
00:26:22,167 --> 00:26:24,200
72款的。改过。
'72. Tweaked.

502
00:26:24,233 --> 00:26:27,700
开一辆改装过的351一脚油门踩到底，肠子都能给你甩进后兜里。
Flooring the gas on a tweaked
351, you'll still put your
bowels in your back pocket.

503
00:26:27,733 --> 00:26:28,867
可不是嘛！
Tell me about it!

504
00:26:28,900 --> 00:26:30,800
那咱们这就去捉耗子吧，绅士们？
Shall we hunt some rodent,
then, gents?

505
00:26:31,667 --> 00:26:33,167
他进去了！
There he goes!

506
00:26:34,367 --> 00:26:35,533
所以，呃……
So, um...

507
00:26:38,867 --> 00:26:41,900
好吧……那这货演的是谁啊？
Well... Who's that, then?

508
00:26:41,933 --> 00:26:44,233
呃，他叫杰罗姆·威尔逊。
Well, he's called
Jerome Wilson.

509
00:26:44,267 --> 00:26:45,533
（全场大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

510
00:26:45,567 --> 00:26:48,467
所以……后来有人跟我提了一嘴
So...so... Someone pointed out
to me afterwards

511
00:26:48,467 --> 00:26:51,667
说这人长得有点像你，这纯属巧合哈。
that it reminded him
a bit of you,
which is pure coincidence.

512
00:26:51,700 --> 00:26:53,233
那我真是倍感荣幸、受宠若惊啊。
I'm very flattered
and honoured.

513
00:26:53,267 --> 00:26:55,933
我本来还打算找你来演的。
I was going to
ask you to do it.

514
00:26:55,967 --> 00:26:57,733
我本来想让你在剧里本色出演。
I was going to ask you
to be in it as yourself.

515
00:26:57,767 --> 00:27:01,967
但转念一想，要是你亲自演，我就不好狠下刀子黑你了。
But then I thought I couldn't
quite stick the knife in
if it was you.

516
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,967
这刀子扎得可真够狠够深的，
It's gone in nice
and deep there,

517
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:07,500
因为那片段最后来了一句：“这人挺混球的，不是吗？”
because it does end up with,
"Bit of a dick, isn't he?"

518
00:27:07,533 --> 00:27:09,300
那季最后就是这么收尾的。
It's how that series ends.

519
00:27:09,333 --> 00:27:11,467
不过杰里米，只有当你打心底深爱一样东西，你才能把它讽刺得这么绝。
You can only satirise
something if you
truly love it though, Jeremy.

520
00:27:11,467 --> 00:27:13,467
拉倒吧。因为我老婆坐那儿看的时候，
Well, no. 'Cause my wife sat
watching it,

521
00:27:13,467 --> 00:27:16,633
每当剧情播到我犯浑、像个混蛋的时候，
她就直点头，“对，太对了。”
and when it got to the bit
where I'm a bit of a dick,
she was going, "Yeah. Yeah."

522
00:27:16,667 --> 00:27:18,967
（笑声）
(LAUGHING)

523
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:21,600
你写剧本的方式，最让我佩服的一点，
One of the things I love about
the way you write stuff,

524
00:27:21,633 --> 00:27:24,467
就是你对细节那种极致的讲究。
is how much attention
to detail you always
put into it.

525
00:27:24,467 --> 00:27:26,033
尤其是里面的车。
And particularly the cars.

526
00:27:26,067 --> 00:27:28,067
加雷思·奇斯曼开的是福特Probe，
'Cause Gareth Cheeseman
had the Probe,

527
00:27:28,100 --> 00:27:30,467
帕特里奇开的是……
先是罗孚，后来换成雷克萨斯，
Partridge had the...
Well, the Rover
and then the Lexus,

528
00:27:30,467 --> 00:27:32,833
两台车都绝了，
完全就是他那种人的味儿。
both, you know,
spot on for him.

529
00:27:32,867 --> 00:27:35,967
现在萨克森代尔又开上了野马。
And now Saxondale
has got the Mustang.

530
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:39,767
我是说，这车选得简直绝了。
I mean, that's just
a brilliant piece of casting.

531
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:41,633
这方面我当时挑剔得很。
Well, I was very
specific about it.

532
00:27:41,667 --> 00:27:43,800
聊到这儿，咱们车迷龟毛较真的毛病就犯了，
This is where we get really
kind of, anal about cars,

533
00:27:43,833 --> 00:27:48,500
但我当时不想要《警网铁金刚》里那种
GT Fastback快背版野马……
but I didn't want, sort of,
the GT Fastback Mustang
from Bullitt...

534
00:27:48,533 --> 00:27:50,633
对，史蒂夫·麦昆开的那台，太帅太酷了。
No, that Steve McQueen drove.
That's too cool.

535
00:27:50,667 --> 00:27:52,467
- 克拉克森：搭载390引擎的那台。
- 没错。
-CLARKSON: The 390.
-That's right.

536
00:27:52,467 --> 00:27:54,933
你看，懂行啊，说得好。
See, good. Well done.

537
00:27:54,967 --> 00:28:01,033
所以呢，呃……
我想要的是那台Boss 351……
So, um...
I wanted the Boss 351, uh...

538
00:28:01,067 --> 00:28:02,367
就是邦德电影里的那台……
That's the Bond one from...

539
00:28:02,467 --> 00:28:04,100
《007之金刚钻》里的那一台，
It's the one from
Diamonds Are Forever,

540
00:28:04,133 --> 00:28:06,300
两轮侧立着穿过窄巷的那台。
that goes sideways
on its side wheels
through that alleyway.

541
00:28:06,333 --> 00:28:08,900
但……那场戏穿帮了。
But... There's a continuity
error in it.

542
00:28:08,933 --> 00:28:10,833
呃，算穿帮，也不算。
Well, there is
and there isn't.

543
00:28:10,867 --> 00:28:12,767
- 我知道这个穿帮！
- 行啊，你说说看。
-I know about this.
-Go on, then.

544
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:15,967
行，当年他们拍007电影
《金刚钻》的时候，
Okay, when they did
the James Bond film
Diamonds Are Forever,

545
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:18,067
留下了影史上最著名的穿帮镜头之一。
there is one of the most
famous mistakes on film.

546
00:28:18,100 --> 00:28:21,500
车子开进小巷时，
是靠这边的侧轮立起来，像这样。
The car goes through
on its wheels that way,
like that.

547
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:25,067
结果等从小巷开出来的时候，
居然换成了另一边的侧轮！
And then, when it comes out
of the alley,
it's the other way round.

548
00:28:25,100 --> 00:28:26,667
- 没错。
- 所以他们干了什么呢，
-Yeah.
-So what they do is,

549
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:29,500
他们在中间硬插了一个
他在车里开车的镜头。
they put in a shot
in the middle
with him driving along.

550
00:28:29,533 --> 00:28:32,000
突然那车就……
你在车里看到他们晃过来……
Suddenly the car goes...
You see them in the car,
going...

551
00:28:32,033 --> 00:28:33,833
然后车子（嘎吱一声）——
And it goes (CREAKS)

552
00:28:33,867 --> 00:28:35,533
搞得好像……
As if somehow...

553
00:28:35,567 --> 00:28:39,133
要是它在巷子里能这么来回翻，
那直接正常开过去不就得了！
If it could do that,
it could drive
through the gap normally!

554
00:28:39,900 --> 00:28:41,200
那段简直是我最爱看的地方。
That was my favourite bit.

555
00:28:41,233 --> 00:28:43,900
你完全能想象剪辑师在机房里哀嚎：“天哪，惨了。”
You can see them in
the edit going, "Oh, dear."

556
00:28:43,933 --> 00:28:45,100
- “完了！”
- “完了！”
-"Oh, no!"
-"Oh, no!"

557
00:28:45,133 --> 00:28:47,033
我当时还以为他们会这么搞……
I thought they
might do this...

558
00:28:47,067 --> 00:28:50,167
真的……我还以为他们会直接把画面水平翻转镜像。
This is really... I thought
they might flip the image.

559
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:54,233
但开出来的地方路标太多了，
那可是在拉斯维加斯，
But when he drives out,
there's lots of signs, uh,
it's Las Vegas

560
00:28:54,267 --> 00:28:56,967
旁边全是大赌场，
一翻转招牌全成反字了，所以……
and there's casino here
and all the signs would be
backwards, so...

561
00:28:57,000 --> 00:29:00,700
我能就这个再说个极其龟毛的冷知识吗？
你肯定爱听。
Can I give you a really
anal one on that?
You'll like this.

562
00:29:00,733 --> 00:29:03,200
你知道吧，在那些全球投放的
汽车广告里，
You know, in car adverts
that are run
all round the world,

563
00:29:03,233 --> 00:29:07,467
经常能看到其中一个车牌号是
YHY 101。
there's one of
the number plates is
YHY 101.

564
00:29:07,467 --> 00:29:10,233
这么做是为了镜像翻转画面
做成左舵或右舵版本时，
It's so that when they flip it
to make it left
or right hand drive,

565
00:29:10,267 --> 00:29:12,367
车牌看起来依然没毛病。
the number plate
still makes sense.

566
00:29:14,100 --> 00:29:15,767
我挺喜欢这个冷知识。
I like that fact.

567
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:19,700
以后参加晚宴要是冷场了，
我可以用它来打破尴尬。
I might use that
a dinner party when there's
an awkward pause.

568
00:29:19,733 --> 00:29:22,167
（笑）对，我也……
(LAUGHING) Yes, I do...

569
00:29:22,200 --> 00:29:24,467
然后全场陷入更可怕的死寂！
And then the pause
is even longer!

570
00:29:25,467 --> 00:29:27,100
现在来看圈速。
Now the lap.

571
00:29:27,133 --> 00:29:28,933
天呐……
Oh, God...

572
00:29:28,967 --> 00:29:31,833
最搞笑的是，好吧，罗伯·布莱顿，
算得上是你的门生了……
What's really funny, okay,
is Rob Brydon,
who's your protege, really...

573
00:29:31,867 --> 00:29:33,733
（叹气）我知道。
(SIGHS) I know.

574
00:29:33,767 --> 00:29:37,467
他有着上过本节目的所有人里，
最惨不忍睹的用车史。
He has the most wretched
car history of anyone
who's ever been on the show.

575
00:29:37,467 --> 00:29:40,833
他的座驾巅峰居然是一辆骑士（Cavalier），
而且他居然还挺喜欢！
His highlight
was his Cavalier,
and he liked it!

576
00:29:40,867 --> 00:29:42,333
可他当年跑得比你快。
And he was faster than you.

577
00:29:42,367 --> 00:29:45,267
我知道，你知道吗，
那大概是……
I know, do you know,
that's probably the most...

578
00:29:45,300 --> 00:29:48,267
实话说，那真是我人生中
最黑暗的一刻。
That was the worst moment
in my life, actually.

579
00:29:48,300 --> 00:29:51,467
当我得知……来我家干活的泥瓦匠
跑来告诉我：
When I heard... My builder
who came round
to my house, told me,

580
00:29:51,467 --> 00:29:54,367
“你那哥们儿罗伯·布莱顿，
把你按在地上摩擦了。”
"Your mate, Rob Brydon,
he wiped the floor with you."

581
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:55,633
“你说什么？”
"What do you mean?"

582
00:29:55,667 --> 00:29:57,667
-“他圈速比你快。”
-“不可能，绝不可能。”
-"He was faster."
-"No. No. No."

583
00:29:57,700 --> 00:29:59,600
然后我打电话给他问：
“罗伯·布莱顿真的比我快吗？”
Then I rang him, and said
"Was Rob Brydon
faster than me?"

584
00:29:59,633 --> 00:30:01,767
从那之后他就一直拿这事儿
来挤兑我。
And he never
lets me forget that.

585
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,167
每次我一碰到他，他就说，呃，
When I see him, he goes, um,

586
00:30:03,200 --> 00:30:05,533
“史蒂夫，不知道你还记不记得，
"I don't know if you
remember, Steve,

587
00:30:05,567 --> 00:30:07,600
“我当年其实比你
稍微快那么一丁点。”
"I was actually slightly
faster than you."

588
00:30:09,633 --> 00:30:12,700
那么，呃，圈速成绩。
So, um, lap.

589
00:30:12,733 --> 00:30:13,800
今天跑得怎么样？
How did it go on today?

590
00:30:13,833 --> 00:30:15,800
开这辆全新的廉价车？
The new,
reasonably priced car?

591
00:30:15,833 --> 00:30:20,967
呃，我觉得吧……有人跟我说过，
其实是斯提格跟我说的，
I, er, I suppose...
Someone said to me,
actually the Stig said to me,

592
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:24,533
说搞体育的运动员，
that people who are sportsmen

593
00:30:24,567 --> 00:30:27,067
还有搞技术的那帮人，
如果你非要这么分类的话，
and people who are,
if you're like,
technical people,

594
00:30:27,100 --> 00:30:31,533
往往跑得更好，
因为他们更听劝。
tend to do better
because they listen more.

595
00:30:31,567 --> 00:30:32,933
我觉得自己不算那类人，
我有点……
And I don't think,
I'm sort of...

596
00:30:32,967 --> 00:30:34,867
我更偏向于
“别废话，放我上去冲”。
I'm more a sort of,
"Let me just go."

597
00:30:34,900 --> 00:30:37,400
所以我大概不是那种
最守纪律的……
So I'm probably not
the most disciplined...

598
00:30:37,433 --> 00:30:41,367
嗯，从你其中一圈练习赛来看，
这确实有充分的铁证。
Well, there was certainly
evidence of that on one
of your practice laps.

599
00:30:41,400 --> 00:30:42,733
谁想看那段画面？
Who'd like to see that?

600
00:30:42,767 --> 00:30:43,900
观众：想看！
AUDIENCE: Yes!

601
00:30:43,933 --> 00:30:45,400
那咱们来看看录像吧。
Let's run the tape then.

602
00:30:45,433 --> 00:30:47,467
来喽。
这儿就是先稍微
练上两圈。
Here we go.
Just a little bit
of practice here.

603
00:30:47,500 --> 00:30:49,733
颠起来了。
噢，你看你看，
车尾甩出去了，
It's bounced.
Oh, now you see,
you've got your tail out,

604
00:30:49,767 --> 00:30:51,833
差点就救回来了，然后……
哎哟喂！
nearly held it and then,
oh dear!

605
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:58,067
（哔——）软趴趴的破悬挂。
(BLEEPS) Soft suspension.

606
00:30:58,100 --> 00:30:59,067
（观众鼓掌）
(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)

607
00:30:59,100 --> 00:31:01,067
克拉克森：太精彩了！
CLARKSON: Very good!

608
00:31:06,067 --> 00:31:08,667
其实开着还挺爽的。
（轻笑）
It was quite enjoyable,
actually. (CHUCKLES)

609
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:10,333
那咱们来看看你的正赛圈？
Well, shall we see your lap?

610
00:31:10,367 --> 00:31:11,800
-好啊，放吧。
-大家想不想看？
-Yeah, go on.
-Would you like to see that?

611
00:31:11,833 --> 00:31:14,800
-观众：想！
-来喽，上录像。
-AUDIENCE: Yeah!
-Here we go. Play the tape.

612
00:31:14,833 --> 00:31:16,267
发车了！
And we're off.

613
00:31:18,633 --> 00:31:21,467
求求老天，千万让我比
罗伯·布莱顿快。求你了！
Please let me be better
than Rob Brydon. Please!

614
00:31:23,533 --> 00:31:26,167
克拉克森：你这弯切过了，
但车滑了一下，
倒也无所谓了，
CLARKSON: You cut that corner
but that skidded,
so it doesn't matter,

615
00:31:26,200 --> 00:31:28,567
谁让你切弯呢，
切弯就会这样。
that's what it does
if you cut the corner.

616
00:31:28,600 --> 00:31:30,567
（长舒一口气）
(EXHALES LOUDLY)

617
00:31:32,633 --> 00:31:35,600
噢，过得又紧又顺。
这把漂亮。
Oh, that's nice and tight
through there. I like that.

618
00:31:35,633 --> 00:31:38,467
（哔——）我的二挡……（哔——）
(BLEEPS) My second... (BLEEPS)

619
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:40,567
克拉克森：刚才离边缘有点险啊。
CLARKSON: A bit close there.

620
00:31:42,467 --> 00:31:45,967
突然之间，
阿兰·帕特里奇
夺过了方向盘。
Suddenly Alan Partridge
has taken over
the wheel there.

621
00:31:47,867 --> 00:31:50,500
原来那根本不是喜剧虚构角色，
那就是你本人啊。
And it wasn't really
a comic creation, it was you.

622
00:31:50,533 --> 00:31:52,467
史蒂夫·库根：可不是嘛，我知道。
STEVE COOGAN: Yeah, I know.

623
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:54,500
再快点！
Go faster!

624
00:31:54,533 --> 00:31:57,533
克拉克森：你眼睛
可没少死盯着挡把看啊。
CLARKSON: There's a lot of
staring at the gear lever
going on.

625
00:31:57,567 --> 00:31:59,467
-布莱恩·考克斯当时也……
-这挡把烦死我了。
-Brian Cox was doing that...
-It was annoying me.

626
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:02,300
克拉克森：……上周死盯着它，
指望用意念能把挡……噢！
CLARKSON: ...last week
staring at it in the hope
that he could make... Ooh!

627
00:32:03,767 --> 00:32:05,600
这下真够猛的。
That was violent.

628
00:32:05,633 --> 00:32:07,867
现在到了……
噢，这弯连打了两把方向。
Now we're here at a bit of...
Oh, two turn ins for that
corner in a row.

629
00:32:07,900 --> 00:32:11,500
这下够胆大、够凶，
直接压草过去，
控制得很稳。
That's nice and brave,
across the grass,
kept it on there nicely.

630
00:32:11,533 --> 00:32:13,967
甘本弯……
借着这股劲保持甩尾。
Gambon...
Using that to keep
the tail out.

631
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,500
冲线啦！
And there we are
across the line!

632
00:32:22,133 --> 00:32:24,467
那你觉得你能排第几？
Where do you reckon, then?

633
00:32:24,800 --> 00:32:26,233
我可能……
I've maybe...

634
00:32:26,267 --> 00:32:28,500
我觉得怎么也能
排在迈克尔·甘本前面吧。
I'd like to think
I'd be above Michael Gambon.

635
00:32:28,533 --> 00:32:30,800
-克拉克森：我能跟你说句实话吗？
-说吧。
-CLARKSON: Now, can I
just be honest with you?
-Yeah, go on.

636
00:32:30,833 --> 00:32:36,767
斯提格说，他觉得
这大热天可能把你脑子
给热出什么毛病了……
The Stig said he thinks
that the heat might have
done something to you...

637
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:38,200
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

638
00:32:38,233 --> 00:32:40,933
要么就是把车或者赛道给晒抽了。
Or the car or the track
or something.

639
00:32:40,967 --> 00:32:43,800
因为他居然对你的车技赞不绝口。
'Cause he was very flattering
about your driving.

640
00:32:43,833 --> 00:32:48,000
真的，他说你开得非常棒，
技术扎实，晚刹车，攻势凶猛……
He did, he said you were
very good, competent,
late braking, aggressive...

641
00:32:48,033 --> 00:32:50,033
动作全都很到位。
All of the right things.

642
00:32:52,067 --> 00:32:54,633
但就是……不快……
But, not quick...

643
00:32:54,667 --> 00:32:56,933
讲句扎心的实话……1分……
To be brutal... One minute...

644
00:32:58,233 --> 00:33:00,700
50秒9。
50.9 seconds.

645
00:33:00,733 --> 00:33:04,167
所以排在这儿。不过大家还是
给点掌声吧！
So it's there. But give him
a round of applause.

646
00:33:08,467 --> 00:33:09,900
这样，我给你个特殊待遇。
I'll tell you what I'll do.

647
00:33:14,467 --> 00:33:16,467
史无前例头一遭——“酷热”。
The first one ever - hot.

648
00:33:17,967 --> 00:33:20,300
不是说圈速火热，
我说的是气温。
That's not the lap.
That's the temperature.

649
00:33:20,333 --> 00:33:22,233
但你想听真正残酷的噩耗吗？
But do you want to know
the really bad thing?

650
00:33:22,267 --> 00:33:24,133
也许……我真不该告诉你。
Perhaps, I shouldn't
tell you this.

651
00:33:24,967 --> 00:33:28,033
罗伯·布莱顿……
Rob Brydon...

652
00:33:28,067 --> 00:33:31,867
开着那辆马力更小、更破的旧车，
都比你快。
-还快。
In the old, less powerful car
was quicker.
-Quicker.

653
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:35,100
居然还是比罗伯慢？
It's still slower than Rob?

654
00:33:35,133 --> 00:33:38,233
没错。要不你今晚就睡这儿算了？
Yeah. Would you like to
stay the night here?

655
00:33:38,267 --> 00:33:39,567
（叹气）
(SIGHS)

656
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:42,133
记得关机……（笑）
Turn your phone... (LAUGHS)

657
00:33:42,167 --> 00:33:44,900
女士们先生们，
史蒂夫·库根！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Steve Coogan!

658
00:33:44,933 --> 00:33:47,333
（观众欢呼喝彩）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

659
00:33:51,233 --> 00:33:53,567
好了……话说回来……
Now... Now...

660
00:33:53,600 --> 00:33:56,800
以前你要是想买一辆
优秀的小型车，
In the olden days,
if you wanted
a great, small car,

661
00:33:56,833 --> 00:34:01,033
最靠谱的选择
莫过于买辆标致小车。
you really couldn't do
much better than
buy a small Peugeot.

662
00:34:01,067 --> 00:34:04,367
但这几年，
他们脑子好像彻底短路了。
But in recent years,
they seem to have
lost the plot.

663
00:34:04,467 --> 00:34:06,000
没错，就拿206来说。
Yeah, Take the 206.

664
00:34:06,033 --> 00:34:08,367
你当初肯掏钱买它，纯粹是因为
它是在英国本土造的。
You'd only have bought one
because it was made
in Britain.

665
00:34:08,467 --> 00:34:10,633
可现在他们把考文垂工厂给关了，
But now they've closed
that factory in Coventry

666
00:34:10,667 --> 00:34:13,333
以后要搬去土库曼斯坦
还是什么鬼地方生产。
and it's going to be made in
Turkmenistan or somewhere.

667
00:34:13,367 --> 00:34:17,733
一点没错，所以它现在成了一辆
被粗制滥造的烂车。
Exactly, so now it's gonna be
a bad car made badly.

668
00:34:17,767 --> 00:34:21,967
不过不管怎样，标致又推出了一款新小型车，
我替大家去开了一圈。
But anyway, Peugeot have
launched a new small car
and I've been driving it.

669
00:34:28,567 --> 00:34:34,000
瞧，就是这辆。它叫标致207，
也是标致造过块头最大的“小型车”。
Here it is. It's called
the 207 and it's Peugeot's
biggest small car yet.

670
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:40,933
显而易见，
这车长得相当漂亮。
As we can see,
it's a very pretty car.

671
