00:44:58,267 --> 00:45:00,300
废话连篇，根本用不着。
Rubbish. Don't need that.

803
00:45:00,333 --> 00:45:03,567
斯提格要赶465英里的路，
The Stig had
465 miles to cover

804
00:45:03,600 --> 00:45:05,867
而且一副使命必达、全速前进的架势。
and was a man on a mission.

805
00:45:05,900 --> 00:45:08,267
然而詹姆斯这边，完全不是这么回事。
James, however, wasn't.

806
00:45:08,300 --> 00:45:11,367
……一个内径八分之三英寸的隔套衬套，
...a spacer bush
3/8ths internal diameter,

807
00:45:11,467 --> 00:45:13,700
外径半英寸……
half an inch
outside diameter...

808
00:45:13,733 --> 00:45:15,033
这个……
This...

809
00:45:19,267 --> 00:45:24,600
……从后安装支架，使用三号螺栓，
从安装座前方穿入。
...from the rear mount using
bolts three, inserted from
the front of the mounting.

810
00:45:24,633 --> 00:45:29,267
（大喊）詹姆斯，到底要不要垫圈，
要还是不要？！
(LOUDLY) James, does it need
a washer, yes or no?

811
00:45:33,633 --> 00:45:35,467
克拉克森：你手脚必须比现在快点。
CLARKSON: You've got to be
faster than you are being.

812
00:45:35,467 --> 00:45:38,067
今天速度才是王道，
说真的。
Speed is what matters today.
Seriously.

813
00:45:38,100 --> 00:45:40,500
-靠蒙，然后搞快点。
-梅：闭嘴，杰里米。
-Guess and go fast.
-MAY: Shut up, Jeremy.

814
00:45:42,500 --> 00:45:44,500
克拉克森：幸运的是，我们确实有一项优势。
CLARKSON: Luckily, we did have
one advantage.

815
00:45:44,533 --> 00:45:47,367
斯提格不肯绕行M25环城高速，
The Stig had refused
to go round the M25

816
00:45:47,467 --> 00:45:50,700
非要一头扎进伦敦市中心
笔直横穿过去……
and was ploughing
straight through the middle
of London...

817
00:45:50,733 --> 00:45:53,033
而且还是晚高峰。
At rush hour.

818
00:45:53,067 --> 00:45:55,100
他干嘛非要那么走？
肯定是因为……
Why is he doing that?
It must be...

819
00:45:55,133 --> 00:45:57,533
“我就要按直线走，
我可是斯提格。”
I am going as the crow flies,
I am a Stig.

820
00:45:57,567 --> 00:45:59,467
哈蒙德：“走直线，老子绝不偏航。”
HAMMOND: Straight line,
I will not deviate.

821
00:46:02,767 --> 00:46:05,167
趁他被堵着，我们像疯子一样拼命干。
While he's stopped,
we work like mad men.

822
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:07,500
克拉克森：对嘛，这才是干活的样子！
CLARKSON: Now, that's what
I'm talking about.

823
00:46:08,467 --> 00:46:10,233
瞧瞧什么叫造车。
How to build a car.

824
00:46:14,467 --> 00:46:15,700
断了。
It's broken.

825
00:46:15,733 --> 00:46:17,600
-梅：别拿锤子砸。
-为什么？
-MAY: Don't hit it
with a hammer.
-Why?

826
00:46:17,633 --> 00:46:19,567
梅：因为那是粗鄙混混才用的工具。
MAY: 'Cause it's a tool
of a pikey.

827
00:46:23,467 --> 00:46:27,567
所以你要是买零件自己组装，
只要一万五千镑，对吧？
So if you buy it in this state
and build it yourself,
it's 15,000, okay?

828
00:46:27,600 --> 00:46:32,000
要是买组装好的整车，就像斯提格开的那辆，
就得多掏两千五百镑。
If you buy it ready-built,
like the Stig's,
it's £2,500 more.

829
00:46:32,033 --> 00:46:33,733
想想自己动手的乐趣。
Think of the fun
of assembling.

830
00:46:33,767 --> 00:46:35,100
干这破事哪来的乐趣！
It's not fun to do this.

831
00:46:35,133 --> 00:46:37,467
你老婆跟人跑了，在跟送奶工滚床单，
Your wife leaves you,
she's in bed with a milkman.

832
00:46:37,467 --> 00:46:41,633
而你还在那儿喊：
“我的前悬挂组件跑哪儿去了？！”
And you're,
"Where's my front
suspension unit?"

833
00:46:41,667 --> 00:46:45,633
克拉克森：
斯提格花了整整90分钟才穿过伦敦南部。
CLARKSON:
It took Stig 90 minutes
to get across south London.

834
00:46:45,667 --> 00:46:48,333
我看他动弹了，
应该正在过泰晤士河。
I think he's moved.
I think he's crossing
the River Thames.

835
00:46:49,233 --> 00:46:51,267
而我们充分利用了这段时间。
And we had used the time well.

836
00:46:51,300 --> 00:46:54,467
一个半小时，后悬挂装好了，
One and a half hours,
the rear suspension is on,

837
00:46:54,467 --> 00:46:57,767
后刹车、传动轴，那边全齐活了。
rear brakes, drive shaft,
everything done there.

838
00:46:57,800 --> 00:47:01,533
前头这角，坦白讲，
简直是一项壮举。
Up front, this corner,
a magnificent achievement,
frankly.

839
00:47:01,567 --> 00:47:03,733
一切运转正……
你干嘛呢？
Everything working...
What are you doing?

840
00:47:03,767 --> 00:47:05,933
得把转向机夹紧固定住。
We have to clamp
the steering rack down.

841
00:47:05,967 --> 00:47:07,467
哎，我早就知道。
Oh, I knew that.

842
00:47:08,933 --> 00:47:11,700
詹姆斯，我能开始搞内饰了吗？
James, can I start
on the interior.

843
00:47:11,733 --> 00:47:13,033
我觉得这主意棒极了。
I think that's
an excellent idea.

844
00:47:13,067 --> 00:47:14,367
我这就去拿把锤子。
I'll get a hammer.

845
00:47:17,500 --> 00:47:21,000
于是在理查德和詹姆斯
忙着对付转向齿条的时候，
So while Richard and James
busied themselves
with the steering rack,

846
00:47:21,033 --> 00:47:23,033
我开始死磕座椅了。
I tackled the seats.

847
00:47:24,300 --> 00:47:26,100
（哈蒙德嘟囔声）
(HAMMOND MUMBLING)

848
00:47:26,133 --> 00:47:29,233
原厂出厂时根本没对齐，
但我现在搞定了，简直完美。
They hadn't lined them up
in the factory,
but I have now, brilliantly.

849
00:47:38,467 --> 00:47:42,200
克拉克森：
斯提格此时上了M40高速，
油门踩到底一路狂飙。
CLARKSON:
The Stig was now on the M40
and had the hammer down.

850
00:47:42,233 --> 00:47:45,800
而我也放下了我的锤子，
拿起了扳手。
I too had put my hammer down,
and picked up a spanner.

851
00:47:45,833 --> 00:47:47,933
不过，注定要出幺蛾子。
Though something
was bound to go wrong.

852
00:47:47,967 --> 00:47:49,500
我怎么弄成这样的？
How did I do that?

853
00:47:49,533 --> 00:47:51,533
还不是因为你
直接往里一扔看都不看。
You did it 'cause
you just dumped it
and didn't look.

854
00:47:51,567 --> 00:47:53,033
而且还滑到底下去了。
And slid underneath.

855
00:47:54,533 --> 00:47:55,933
（梅轻笑）
(MAY CHUCKLES)

856
00:47:55,967 --> 00:47:57,367
-我还得重新把它拆出来吗？
-必须拆。
-Have I got to
take it out again?
-You have to.

857
00:47:57,467 --> 00:47:58,533
让咱们琢磨琢磨。
Let's think about it.

858
00:47:59,667 --> 00:48:02,900
梅：没关系，
斯提格还在400英里开外呢。
MAY: No matter,
the Stig was still
400 miles away.

859
00:48:02,933 --> 00:48:04,600
而且他又停下来了。
and coming to a halt again.

860
00:48:04,633 --> 00:48:08,667
这次停在了
牛津服务区。
This time
at the Oxford services.

861
00:48:08,700 --> 00:48:10,533
克拉克森：他在牛津，
而我们正在往里装发动机。
CLARKSON: He's at Oxford
and we're putting
the engine in.

862
00:48:10,567 --> 00:48:11,767
到了发动机登场时刻！
It is engine time.

863
00:48:11,800 --> 00:48:13,500
胜利属于我们！
Victory is ours!

864
00:48:18,733 --> 00:48:20,267
梅：与此同时，
南边的牛津，
MAY: Meanwhile,
down in Oxford,

865
00:48:20,300 --> 00:48:23,467
斯提格暴露出关于他的新秘密。
the Stig was revealing
something new about himself.

866
00:48:25,467 --> 00:48:26,667
梅：啊！
MAY: Ah!

867
00:48:26,700 --> 00:48:28,233
（哈蒙德大笑）
(HAMMOND LAUGHS)

868
00:48:29,133 --> 00:48:31,367
他居然长了膀胱。
He has a bladder.

869
00:48:33,167 --> 00:48:35,467
（喧闹声）
(CLAMOURING)

870
00:48:35,467 --> 00:48:37,333
对对对，就是干那个用的。
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's what it's for.

871
00:48:37,367 --> 00:48:38,467
快去把变速箱拿过来。
Just get the gear box.

872
00:48:43,033 --> 00:48:44,600
-呃……
-克拉克森：怎么了？
-Um...
-CLARKSON: What?

873
00:48:44,633 --> 00:48:45,767
发动机？
Engine?

874
00:48:45,800 --> 00:48:47,900
克拉克森：发动机！
哈蒙德：车！
CLARKSON: Engine!
HAMMOND: Car!

875
00:48:47,933 --> 00:48:50,367
你好啊，斯提格先生，
想一起来吗？
Hello, Stig, sir,
would you like to join?

876
00:48:51,167 --> 00:48:52,600
你得把这个绕过……
You've got to get
this round...

877
00:48:52,633 --> 00:48:53,833
梅：对，没错……
MAY: Yeah, exactly...

878
00:48:53,867 --> 00:48:55,267
哈蒙德：不要啊！
HAMMOND: No!

879
00:49:02,067 --> 00:49:03,467
梅：斯提格到哪儿了？
MAY: Where's the Stig?

880
00:49:05,733 --> 00:49:07,267
克拉克森：这到底怪谁？
CLARKSON: Whose fault
was that?

881
00:49:07,300 --> 00:49:09,233
噢，这下可帮大忙了，对吧？
Oh, that's not
going to help, is it?

882
00:49:13,133 --> 00:49:15,700
克拉克森：刹车盘有多结实？
梅：相当结实。
CLARKSON: How strong
are brake discs?
MAY: Pretty strong.

883
00:49:15,733 --> 00:49:17,467
哈蒙德：挺结实的。
HAMMOND: Quite strong.

884
00:49:17,467 --> 00:49:19,900
结实到能撑得住一整辆车吗？
Are they strong enough
to withstand a car?

885
00:49:19,933 --> 00:49:22,600
哈蒙德：撑不住。
HAMMOND: No.

886
00:49:22,633 --> 00:49:25,167
还记得刚才我钻在车底下装座椅时，
You know
when I was underneath,
putting the seat,

887
00:49:25,200 --> 00:49:29,033
我特意问了句：
“它会不会从支架上掉下来？”
and I specifically said,
"Can it fall off its things?"

888
00:49:29,067 --> 00:49:30,567
结果你说：“不会。”
And you said, "No."

889
00:49:30,600 --> 00:49:32,100
真可惜，当时它居然没砸下来。
And what a shame it didn't.

890
00:49:36,800 --> 00:49:39,967
快点！搞快点！
我要把车放下去了！
Quickly! Quickly!
I'm going to drop the car!

891
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:41,633
哈蒙德：你说得对。
HAMMOND: You're right.

892
00:49:41,667 --> 00:49:43,000
搞定，行了。
There you go.

893
00:49:43,033 --> 00:49:45,233
-（大笑）
-皆大欢喜。
-(LAUGHS)
-Everybody's happy.

894
00:49:45,267 --> 00:49:47,533
克拉克森：此时此刻，斯提格已经快到伯明翰了。
CLARKSON: By now, the Stig
was nearing Birmingham.

895
00:49:47,567 --> 00:49:51,367
我们浪费了太多时间，
可我们的发动机依然塞不进去。
We'd lost time
and our engine still
wouldn't go in.

896
00:49:51,467 --> 00:49:53,300
-你知道问题出在哪儿吗？
-哪儿？
-You know what the problem is?
-What?

897
00:49:53,467 --> 00:49:56,967
因为这破车库建得歪七扭八的，
整块地都是个斜坡……
Because the garage
is built on the cock,
and is all on a slope...

898
00:49:57,000 --> 00:49:59,667
-嗯。
-我们得把车头朝向那边才行。
-Hmm.
-We really need the car
pointing that way.

899
00:49:59,700 --> 00:50:01,933
詹姆斯，我们没时间了，
得先把发动机移出来，
James, we haven't got time,
we have to move
the engine out,

900
00:50:01,967 --> 00:50:03,533
把整辆车掉个头，
还得挪千斤顶。
turn the whole car round,
move the jacks.

901
00:50:03,567 --> 00:50:06,800
你看，他马上就要上M42高速了。
说真的……
Look, he's just about
to get on to the M42.
Seriously...

902
00:50:09,433 --> 00:50:12,467
克拉克森：真叫人不爽，
这个弹钢琴的居然说对了。
CLARKSON: Annoyingly,
the pianist was right.

903
00:50:12,500 --> 00:50:16,067
詹姆斯，告诉我该怎么做，
我来把它往下压。
James, tell me what to do
and I'll push it down.

904
00:50:16,100 --> 00:50:17,867
哈蒙德：没事，我们托得住。
HAMMOND: It's all right,
we've got it.

905
00:50:17,900 --> 00:50:19,967
完全不用管这台死沉的发动机，
还有托着它的小矮子。
Don't worry about
the big heavy engine
and the small guy holding it.

906
00:50:21,867 --> 00:50:24,033
-梅：只要我一喊停，立刻撒手。
-（哈蒙德吃力地闷哼）
-MAY: Be ready to stop
as soon as I say.
-(HAMMOND GRUNTING)

907
00:50:24,067 --> 00:50:25,933
克拉克森：詹姆斯，
看看你背后的地图。
CLARKSON: James,
look at the map
behind you.

908
00:50:25,967 --> 00:50:27,233
是，我知道，杰里米。
Yeah, I know, Jeremy.

909
00:50:27,267 --> 00:50:28,833
哈蒙德：只要……
梅：那你有什么高见？
HAMMOND: Just...
MAY: What are you suggesting?

910
00:50:28,867 --> 00:50:30,833
-难道我们要直接趴在上面压吗？
-咱们能先别内讧斗嘴了吗？
-Should we just
lie on the top?
-Can we not bicker now?

911
00:50:33,833 --> 00:50:34,933
克拉克森：晃一晃它。
CLARKSON: Jiggle it.

912
00:50:34,967 --> 00:50:37,067
哈蒙德：我特么已经吃奶的劲都在晃了！
HAMMOND: I'm jiggling
like a bugger.

913
00:50:37,800 --> 00:50:39,233
现在你可以往下放了。
Now you can go down.

914
00:50:40,700 --> 00:50:42,500
哈蒙德：噢，杰里米！
HAMMOND: Oh, Jeremy!

915
00:50:42,533 --> 00:50:44,067
梅：我的意思又不是让你整把松手！
MAY: I didn't mean
release it all together.

916
00:50:44,100 --> 00:50:46,567
你特么直接把它从车底给砸穿下去了！
You just dropped it
through the bloody car!

917
00:50:53,633 --> 00:50:56,900
他离这儿还有299英里。
He is 299 miles away.

918
00:50:56,933 --> 00:50:59,233
按斯提格的车速，
估计也就一个小时的事。
At Stig's speeds,
that could be an hour.

919
00:51:01,033 --> 00:51:03,267
哈蒙德：杰里米被彻底剥夺了“发动机主管”的职务，
HAMMOND: Jeremy was sacked
from engine management

920
00:51:03,300 --> 00:51:05,600
改由我和詹姆斯亲自动手搞定。
and James and I
did it ourselves.

921
00:51:05,633 --> 00:51:07,167
-塞进去了！
-太棒了！
-It's in!
-Yes!

922
00:51:07,867 --> 00:51:09,467
点火试试！
Start it up!

923
00:51:09,500 --> 00:51:10,867
还没全装好呢。
It's not that in.

924
00:51:12,267 --> 00:51:14,567
-刹车管路全得接上。
-刹车。
-All the brakes
have to be connected up.
-Brakes.

925
00:51:14,600 --> 00:51:16,667
-还有剩下的所有附属配件。
-配件。
-All the rest
of the ancillaries.
-Ancillaries.

926
00:51:16,700 --> 00:51:17,900
-电瓶。
-电瓶。
-Battery.
-Battery.

927
00:51:17,933 --> 00:51:19,200
-节气门连杆。
-油门连杆。
-Throttle linkage.
-Throttle linkage.

928
00:51:19,233 --> 00:51:20,633
-离合连杆。
-离合。
-Clutch linkage.
-Clutch.

929
00:51:20,667 --> 00:51:21,867
-挡位连杆。
-挡位。
-Gear linkage.
-Gears.

930
00:51:21,900 --> 00:51:23,800
说实话，
活儿还多着呢。
There's quite a lot to do
if we're honest.

931
00:51:25,333 --> 00:51:27,233
哈蒙德：就在我们装发动机
搞得焦头烂额时，
HAMMOND: During
our engine fitting
calamity,

932
00:51:27,267 --> 00:51:30,833
斯提格已经把在伦敦
耽搁的时间
全给抢回来了。
the Stig had made up
all the time he'd lost
in London.

933
00:51:30,867 --> 00:51:33,067
现在换我们陷入被动了。
We were now on the back foot.

934
00:51:39,233 --> 00:51:40,133
锤子。
Hammer.

935
00:51:40,167 --> 00:51:41,600
-哈蒙德：别！
-梅：不行！
-HAMMOND: No!
-MAY: No!

936
00:51:47,667 --> 00:51:52,533
我得先把这个装上，
才能把这边另一个东西
装上去？
I have to attach this
before I can attach
something else here?

937
00:51:54,733 --> 00:51:56,667
这意味着接下来
我能装……
That means I can
then attach the...

938
00:51:56,700 --> 00:51:58,267
-防滚架？
-不对！
-Roll bar?
-No!

939
00:52:00,900 --> 00:52:02,533
天哪……
Oh, God...

940
00:52:02,567 --> 00:52:04,167
（金属撞击声）
(METAL CLANGING)

941
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:14,533
梅：看说明书上的图啊。
MAY: Look at the picture.

942
00:52:14,567 --> 00:52:16,100
-克拉克森：这图屁都没说！
-梅：明明写着呢！
-CLARKSON: It doesn't
tell me anything!
-MAY: It does!

943
00:52:16,133 --> 00:52:19,533
克拉克森：他们还不如直接
拍一张你的屁股印上去。
CLARKSON: They may as well
have photographed
your arse.

944
00:52:19,567 --> 00:52:24,033
哈蒙德：斯提格此时已经跑了220英里，
一路顺风顺水。
HAMMOND: The Stig had now
covered 220 miles
and was making good time.

945
00:52:25,567 --> 00:52:28,600
唯一值得庆幸的，
就是他的油箱很小。
The only blessing
was his small fuel tank.

946
00:52:34,233 --> 00:52:36,600
我猜他是停车加油了。
I think he's stopped for fuel.

947
00:52:39,967 --> 00:52:42,167
斯提格以前进站加过油吗？
Has the Stig
ever stopped for fuel before?

948
00:52:45,733 --> 00:52:47,233
他要怎么结账啊？
How will he pay for it?

949
00:52:50,267 --> 00:52:52,200
你有积分卡吗？
You got a Nectar card?

950
00:52:56,000 --> 00:52:59,333
梅：当斯提格风驰电掣
穿过湖区时，
MAY: While the Stig
was powering through
the lake district,

951
00:52:59,367 --> 00:53:02,533
杰里米正在装方向盘。
Jeremy was attaching
the steering wheel.

952
00:53:05,767 --> 00:53:07,567
克拉克森：断了。
CLARKSON: Broken.

953
00:53:07,600 --> 00:53:10,533
梅：紧接着他又开始了
第二次装座椅的尝试。
MAY: And then he had
his second go
at fitting the seats.

954
00:53:10,567 --> 00:53:15,567
烦死了、烦死了、烦死了、
无聊、无聊、
太无聊了、枯燥、
Bored, bored, bored,
bored, bored,
bored, boring,

955
00:53:15,600 --> 00:53:20,200
没劲、乏味、折磨人、
讨厌、腰酸、
胳膊疼、
boring, dull, tedious,
annoying, back ache,
arm ache,

956
00:53:20,233 --> 00:53:23,233
抽筋、难受、
讨厌、詹姆斯……
cramp, miserable,
hate, James...

957
00:53:23,267 --> 00:53:25,567
卡莱尔离苏格兰还有多远？
How far from Scotland
is Carlisle?

958
00:53:28,633 --> 00:53:30,100
克拉克森：搞定了！
CLARKSON: It's finished!

959
00:53:30,133 --> 00:53:31,733
梅：并没搞定。
MAY: No, it wasn't.

960
00:53:31,767 --> 00:53:35,567
梅：杰里米，
在你继续瞎忙活之前，
我能提个意见吗？
MAY: Jeremy,
before you go any further,
can I make a point?

961
00:53:35,600 --> 00:53:38,567
得先把安全带固定好，
才能把座椅装进去。
You have to mount
the harness first,
before you put the seats in.

962
00:53:38,600 --> 00:53:40,067
你逗我呢吧。
You're joking.

963
00:53:42,633 --> 00:53:44,933
我经手的每样东西
都是一坨垃圾。
Every single thing I do
is rubbish.

964
00:53:44,967 --> 00:53:46,633
梅：你干什么都不动脑子。
MAY: You don't think
anything through.

965
00:53:46,667 --> 00:53:48,800
你就是随手一抓，
心想：
“这玩意儿穿过那儿就行。”
You just get a hold of it,
and think,
"That goes through there."

966
00:53:48,833 --> 00:53:50,100
但凡你稍微琢磨一下……
But if you just
thought about it...

967
00:53:50,133 --> 00:53:52,000
这绝对是我这辈子
过得最惨的一天。
This is the worst day
of my life ever.

968
00:53:54,767 --> 00:53:56,167
克拉克森：
斯提格已经杀进苏格兰了。
CLARKSON:
The Stig hit Scotland.

969
00:53:56,200 --> 00:53:58,100
他现在离我们
只剩100英里，
He was now
just 100 miles away

970
00:53:58,133 --> 00:54:01,800
而我们还得搞定
刹车、车身外壳
和整车电路。
and we still had to do
the brakes, the bodywork
and the electrics.

971
00:54:01,833 --> 00:54:04,500
谢天谢地，
理查德和我
抄了点近道！
Thank God
Richard and I had taken
some shortcuts!

972
00:54:04,900 --> 00:54:06,567
（大笑）
(LAUGHS)

973
00:54:10,467 --> 00:54:11,967
杰里米，别啊……
Jeremy, no...

974
00:54:12,000 --> 00:54:14,000
我不装垫圈和螺栓，
这不正省时间嘛。
I'm saving time
by not putting
washers and bolts on.

975
00:54:14,033 --> 00:54:16,367
但是，这些可都是
至关紧要的零件啊。
But, these are all
really important stuff.

976
00:54:16,467 --> 00:54:17,867
我知道，我知道。
I know. I know.

977
00:54:17,900 --> 00:54:19,767
克拉克森：
詹姆斯要是知道了非得气疯。
CLARKSON:
James would flip if he knew.

978
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:24,333
克拉克森：不过不出所料，
詹姆斯正犯着龟毛强迫症，
根本没注意到。
CLARKSON: Predictably, though,
James was being
too anal to notice.

979
00:54:24,367 --> 00:54:27,000
他一整个上午都在干这事：
整理归档。
That's all he's done,
all morning, he files.

980
00:54:27,033 --> 00:54:29,900
把东西拿出来，
再放回去，
然后归档到
He takes stuff out
and then puts it back
and files it

981
00:54:29,933 --> 00:54:31,967
它本该呆的位置。
where it's supposed to be.

982
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:34,133
-（大喊）詹姆斯！
-干嘛？
-(SHOUTS) James!
-What?

983
00:54:34,167 --> 00:54:35,667
别瞎整理了！
Stop filing!

984
00:54:35,700 --> 00:54:37,100
我在找那个该死的套筒，
I'm looking for the
sodding socket thing,

985
00:54:37,133 --> 00:54:38,733
拆那玩意儿必须得用的。
that you need to
take that out.

986
00:54:38,767 --> 00:54:41,100
-你知道在哪儿吗？
你知道在哪儿吗？
-不知道，不知道！
-Do you know where it is?
Do you know where it is?
-No. No!

987
00:54:41,133 --> 00:54:42,500
-你知道它长啥样吗？
-克拉克森：知道！
-Do you know
what it looks like?
-CLARKSON: Yes!

988
00:54:42,533 --> 00:54:44,067
不，你根本不知道。
No, you don't.

989
00:54:45,833 --> 00:54:50,033
哈蒙德：趁着斯提格进站
进行最后一次蜻蜓点水式补能，
HAMMOND: With the Stig pitting
for his final splash and dash,

990
00:54:50,067 --> 00:54:52,667
我们必须开始
给刹车排气，
we had to start
bleeding the brakes,

991
00:54:52,700 --> 00:54:56,933
事实证明，这操作简直处处是
带颜色的荤段子雷区。
which, it turns out,
is a minefield
of double entendres.

992
00:54:56,967 --> 00:54:59,100
“凸头”已经露出来了，
The nipple is off,

993
00:54:59,133 --> 00:55:01,667
管子插进洞里了。
the tube is in the hole.

994
00:55:01,700 --> 00:55:04,467
我需要来几下抽送了。
I will be needing some pump.

995
00:55:04,467 --> 00:55:05,867
梅：他到哪儿了？
克拉克森：把那些扔地上。
MAY: Where is he?
CLARKSON: Put those
on the floor.

996
00:55:05,900 --> 00:55:07,233
-克拉克森：
你怎么拿着那个？
-哦，他……
-CLARKSON:
Why have you got that?
-Oh he's...

997
00:55:07,267 --> 00:55:09,233
他正一路往格拉斯哥开呢。
He's making his way
towards Glasgow.

998
00:55:10,767 --> 00:55:12,767
你现在应该能感觉到它变硬了。
You should feel it
go stiff now.

999
00:55:12,800 --> 00:55:14,467
使劲抽啊，兄弟，快抽！
Pump, man, pump!

1000
00:55:15,633 --> 00:55:16,933
克拉克森：刹车有反应了吗？
CLARKSON: Braking happening?

1001
00:55:16,967 --> 00:55:18,500
噢，对，这下好多了。
嗯，挺结实的。
Oh, yeah, that's much better.
Yeah, that's hard.

1002
00:55:21,233 --> 00:55:25,533
克拉克森：斯提格此时已经下了高速，
正冲着我们杀过来。
CLARKSON: The Stig was now
off the motorway
and bearing down on us.

1003
00:55:25,567 --> 00:55:28,033
灯亮了！
有气儿了！它活过来了！
A light!
It breathes! It lives!

1004
00:55:30,100 --> 00:55:31,667
他过福斯桥了吗？
Has he crossed the Forth yet?

1005
00:55:31,700 --> 00:55:33,100
梅：他正准备
开过去。
MAY: He's just about to
cross it

1006
00:55:33,133 --> 00:55:34,500
哈蒙德：对。
他现在马上就过去了。
正在过。
HAMMOND: Yes.
He's about to now.
He's doing it.

1007
00:55:34,533 --> 00:55:37,633
克拉克森：也就是说，他离我们
只有20英里了。
CLARKSON: That made him
just 20 miles away.

1008
00:55:37,667 --> 00:55:40,033
哈蒙德：我们只剩几分钟了。
快点啊！
HAMMOND: We've got minutes.
Come on!

1009
00:55:42,067 --> 00:55:43,300
汽油。
Petrol.

1010
00:55:43,333 --> 00:55:45,800
正在装挡把头。
开起来总归用得着。
Putting the gear knob on.
It will be required.

1011
00:55:49,033 --> 00:55:50,100
按启动键。
Press the button.

1012
00:55:50,133 --> 00:55:52,333
-（引擎启动声）
-哇哦！（笑）
-(ENGINE STARTS)
-Whoa! (LAUGHS)

1013
00:55:52,367 --> 00:55:55,100
活了！又歇菜了……
It lives! It's dead...

1014
00:55:56,100 --> 00:55:59,600
要是把那个装上，
这车能跑吗？
If that goes on,
will this car work?

1015
00:56:01,933 --> 00:56:03,367
-燃油泵工作了。
-好。
-Fuel pump's working.
-Yes.

1016
00:56:03,467 --> 00:56:04,933
-（引擎启动声）
-漂亮！
-(ENGINE STARTS)
-Well!

1017
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:07,100
-（引擎熄火）
-呃。
-(ENGINE STOPS)
-Oh.

1018
00:56:07,133 --> 00:56:09,200
什么情况？
怎么又熄火了？
What was that?
Why did it do that?

1019
00:56:10,533 --> 00:56:12,333
他只剩五英里了。
He's five miles away.

1020
00:56:14,533 --> 00:56:16,500
（引擎突突异响）
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

1021
00:56:18,500 --> 00:56:20,500
好了好了，
先放一会儿。
Right now,
just leave it a minute.

1022
00:56:21,567 --> 00:56:22,800
现在来。
Now.

1023
00:56:22,833 --> 00:56:25,000
-（引擎启动声）
-哈蒙德：嘿！
-(ENGINE STARTS)
-HAMMOND: Hey!

1024
00:56:25,667 --> 00:56:27,100
（引擎熄火）
(ENGINE STOPS)

1025
00:56:28,033 --> 00:56:30,467
我先把工具收走。
I'm just getting rid of tools.

1026
00:56:38,467 --> 00:56:39,800
梅：谁来开？
MAY: Who's driving?

1027
00:56:39,833 --> 00:56:42,233
-三个人能猜拳吗？
-能啊。
-Can you do it with three?
-Yes.

1028
00:56:42,267 --> 00:56:44,867
-数到一出还是数到三出？
-是数到零出还是数到一出？
-Do we go on one or three?
-We go on not or one?

1029
00:56:44,900 --> 00:56:47,000
我们数“三、二、一，出”，
还是“三、二……”
We go three, two, one, go,
or three, two...

1030
00:56:47,033 --> 00:56:48,767
三、二、一，出！
Three, two, one, go!

1031
00:56:48,800 --> 00:56:51,300
合：三、二、一，出！
ALL: Three, two, one, go!

1032
00:56:51,333 --> 00:56:54,500
-这算什么？
-布包石头。
你来开。
-What does that mean?
-Paper wraps stone.
You're driving.

1033
00:56:54,533 --> 00:56:55,800
走好不送。
Goodbye.

1034
00:56:55,833 --> 00:56:57,900
（引擎突突异响）
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

1035
00:56:57,933 --> 00:56:59,467
固定住燃油泵。
Immobilizing the fuel pump.

1036
00:56:59,467 --> 00:57:01,333
-（引擎启动声）
-哈蒙德：太棒了！
-(ENGINE STARTS)
-HAMMOND: Yes.

1037
00:57:04,800 --> 00:57:07,100
-快快快！
-噢，天呐。
-Come on!
-Oh, God.

1038
00:57:07,133 --> 00:57:10,833
克拉克森：我们要想赢，
唯一的条件
就是冲过起跑线。
CLARKSON: All we had to do
to win
was cross the start line.

1039
00:57:16,933 --> 00:57:19,933
三、二、一……跑！
Three, two, one... Go!

1040
00:57:19,967 --> 00:57:21,267
哈蒙德：漂亮！
HAMMOND: Yes!

1041
00:57:21,300 --> 00:57:23,933
-到此为止！
-搞定，我们赢了！
-That's enough!
-That is it. We won!

1042
00:57:24,567 --> 00:57:26,467
克拉克森：我们赢了，但到底是怎么赢的？
CLARKSON: We had won, but how?

1043
00:57:26,467 --> 00:57:28,067
斯提格身上究竟发生什么事了？
What had happened to the Stig?

1044
00:57:28,100 --> 00:57:30,300
有一阵子
他明明咬得我们死死的。
He was right on top of us
at one point.

1045
00:57:32,733 --> 00:57:34,333
先生，
这辆车是您的吗？
Does this car
belong to you, sir?

1046
00:57:36,767 --> 00:57:38,367
请问
您这是要去哪儿？
Can I ask
where you are going to?

1047
00:57:40,600 --> 00:57:42,233
请问
您是从哪儿过来的？
Can I ask
where you've come from?

1048
00:57:42,267 --> 00:57:46,467
十分钟前
他离这儿可就只有三英里了。
He was three miles away
10 minutes ago.

1049
00:57:46,467 --> 00:57:47,900
先生，这车是偷来的吗？
Is the car stolen, sir?

1050
00:57:49,533 --> 00:57:53,733
我还以为，
哪怕路上堵车
或者进场遇到麻烦……
I would have thought,
even with traffic
or trouble getting in...

1051
00:57:53,767 --> 00:57:56,900
克拉克森：斯提格
保留了
保持沉默的权利。
CLARKSON: The Stig
reserved the right
to remain silent.

1052
00:57:58,933 --> 00:58:00,600
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

1053
00:58:06,067 --> 00:58:07,533
所以……
So...

1054
00:58:07,567 --> 00:58:09,533
瞧见了吧。
There you go.

1055
00:58:09,567 --> 00:58:14,033
事实证明，你完全能在
八小时内攒出一整辆车。
Proof that you can build
an entire car in eight hours.

1056
00:58:14,067 --> 00:58:16,233
确实。
而且讲真，
这其实是件很棒的事。
Absolutely.
And it is actually,
a great thing to do.

1057
00:58:16,267 --> 00:58:18,067
它不像修破烂老车那样，
弄得浑身脏兮兮的。
It's not like
mending an old car,
where it's all dirty.

1058
00:58:18,100 --> 00:58:20,067
所有零件都又干净又崭新。
Everything is clean and new.

1059
00:58:20,100 --> 00:58:21,467
而且组装起来
严丝合缝。
And it all goes
together perfectly.

1060
00:58:21,467 --> 00:58:23,233
体验棒极了，
简直妙不可言。
It's a great experience.
It's wonderful.

1061
00:58:23,267 --> 00:58:27,033
詹姆斯，那我宁愿
把自己的耳朵
用订书机钉在一匹马身上。
James, I would rather
staple my ears
to a horse.

1062
00:58:27,067 --> 00:58:28,900
（观众笑声）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

1063
00:58:28,933 --> 00:58:32,000
说真的，且不说
每隔15分钟你的指关节就得蹭破层皮，
Honestly, apart from the fact
that you chafe your knuckles
every 15 minutes,

1064
00:58:32,033 --> 00:58:33,767
光是花销就吃不消。
there's the expense.

1065
00:58:33,800 --> 00:58:37,500
好吧，买零件散件自己拼，
确实能便宜两千五百英镑。
Okay, it's two
and half thousand pounds
less to buy the car in bits.

1066
00:58:37,533 --> 00:58:41,167
但接下来你得买工具，
然后你还得付离婚赔偿金。
But then you've got to buy
the tools, then you've got
the divorce settlement.

1067
00:58:41,200 --> 00:58:43,067
落得到头来每个周六都得带孩子去吃麦当劳……
End up taking your kids
to McDonalds every Saturday...

1068
00:58:43,100 --> 00:58:47,467
最后你能得到什么？
在场的各位，
有人敢开一辆我亲手造出来的车吗？
And what do you end up with?
Would anybody here
drive a car that I built?

1069
00:58:47,467 --> 00:58:50,300
没人敢，一点没错。
就拿眼前这辆为例吧。
No, exactly.
Let's take this one
as an example.

1070
00:58:50,333 --> 00:58:52,100
这辆就是我们刚攒出来的，对吧？
This is the one
we made, all right?

1071
00:58:52,133 --> 00:58:55,467
我看卡特汉姆那边
在下面这里钉了一块小铭牌。
They've put
a little plaque on it I see,
down here, down at Caterham.

1072
00:58:55,467 --> 00:58:58,500
上面写着：
本车由Top Gear打造。
And this car
built by Top Gear.

1073
00:58:58,533 --> 00:59:01,233
直接让它
变得一文不值。
Which has
rendered it worthless.

1074
00:59:01,267 --> 00:59:03,233
带着这个重磅炸弹，
本期节目就到这里了。
And on that bombshell,
it's time to end.

1075
00:59:03,267 --> 00:59:05,267
非常感谢收看，晚安。
Thank you very much
for watching. Good night.

